# stopCruising(Player player)
# Releases the keyboard. Flips state from cruising to coasting so the
# already-running cruiseTick continues with no input applied — drag and
# gravity decay momentum naturally over ~6-15 ticks. Returns immediately
# (the actual halt happens asynchronously inside the tick loop).
#
# Critically does NOT bump tickGen and does NOT zero velocity. Bumping
# gen would kill the running cruiseTick, leaving nothing to run the
# coast physics. Zeroing velocity reproduces the old jolt-to-stop bug.
#
# Idempotent and safe to call from idle: if neither cruising nor coasting,
# do nothing. Safe to call mid-coast: also a no-op (already coasting).

@using mannequin
@fast

@if !isCruising[player]
    @return
@fi

@var isCruising[player] = false
@var isCoasting[player] = true
